---
// website/src/pages/how-it-works.astro — the run, step by step (website plan, Task W1.4;
// redesign part P8, D185; website changes spec of 2026-10-18, item 4).
//
// The page is the picture and then the detail of it, in that order: the four steps the
// changes spec names (`ArchitectureDiagram.astro`) and, under it, the run README.md's
// `## How it works` numbers, in that section's own words (`RunDetail.astro`). A reader who
// wants the whole of it reads down; a reader who wants the shape of it stops at the picture.
// The changes spec's item 4 asked this page to open with the same drawing the homepage showed
// — one shared component, not two copies — and it still is that component: the owner's
// approved draft of 2026-10-19 ("Home, draft 2 (slider)") is what took the flow off the
// homepage, so this is now the one page that draws it (`src/pages/index.astro`).
//
// Everything else this page could say is a fact of its own: what each stage costs, what it
// can reach, what the caps are. Those are pages and sections of their own (W1.5, W1.6,
// W2.x), and a page that summarised them here would be a second copy of them to keep in step
// (Global Constraint 6). Both components hold every line they render to the document it
// cites at build time.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import ArchitectureDiagram from '../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro'
import RunDetail from '../components/RunDetail.astro'
---

<Base title="How it works">
  <h1 class="page-title">How it works</h1>
  <ArchitectureDiagram />
  <RunDetail />
</Base>

<style>
  /* The page's own title, and the room under it (review round 3, item 3d). This page is the
     picture and then the detail of it, and the picture is what it opens with: `base.css`'s
     heading margin (`--space-xs`, 12 px) left the drawing almost against the title — the
     review measured the gap and found the picture starting 12 px under the `h1`. The room is
     this page's rather than the diagram's, because the drawing sits directly under the `h1`
     here and nowhere else now: the owner's approved draft of 2026-10-19 ("Home, draft 2
     (slider)") took the flow off the homepage, and a margin on the shared component would
     move every page that ever renders it. `website/test/base-styles.mjs` reads this rule and
     refuses a title with a heading's margin under it. */
  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
